<article class="env-lemma" id="0BPY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BPY">Lemma <span data-tag="0BPY">51.7.4</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a Noetherian ring. Let $I \subset A$ be an ideal. Set $Z = V(I)$. Let $n \geq 0$ be an integer. If $H^ i_ Z(A)$ is finite for $0 \leq i \leq n$, then the same is true for $H^ i_ Z(M)$, $0 \leq i \leq n$ for any finite $A$-module $M$ such that $M_ f$ is a finite locally free $A_ f$-module for all $f \in I$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The assumption that $H^ i_ Z(A)$ is finite for $0 \leq i \leq n$ implies there exists an $e \geq 0$ such that $I^ e$ annihilates $H^ i_ Z(A)$ for $0 \leq i \leq n$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/0AW8" data-tag="0AW8">51.7.1</a>. Then Lemma <a href="/tag/0BPX" data-tag="0BPX">51.7.3</a> implies that $H^ i_ Z(M)$, $0 \leq i \leq n$ is annihilated by $I^ m$ for some $m = m(M, i)$. We may take the same $m$ for all $0 \leq i \leq n$. Then Lemma <a href="/tag/0AW8" data-tag="0AW8">51.7.1</a> implies that $H^ i_ Z(M)$ is finite for $0 \leq i \leq n$ as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>